# BDD Testing for ArchiPy Apps

ArchiPy-style apps use **Behave** (not pytest) for acceptance tests.

Live: https://syntaxarc.github.io/ArchiPy/tutorials/testing_strategy/

## Layout

```text
features/
├── *.feature
├── steps/
├── scenario_context.py              # Per-scenario isolated storage
├── scenario_context_pool_manager.py # Scenario ID → ScenarioContext
└── environment.py                   # behave hooks — container setup/teardown
```

Optional extra: `uv add "archipy[behave]"`.

## Ports and Mocks

- Business code depends on ports; steps inject mocks (e.g. `RedisMock`) or real adapters.
- Never import concrete drivers into logics just for tests — swap providers in the DI container / context.

```text
Production:  Logic → RedisAdapter
Test:        Logic → RedisMock
```

## Scenario Isolation

- Use `ScenarioContext` per scenario — no shared mutable globals across scenarios.
- `ScenarioContextPoolManager` creates/retrieves context by scenario ID and disposes after the scenario.

## Infrastructure Tags

Tag scenarios that need Docker/services:

```gherkin
@needs-redis
Scenario: ...
```

Skip when infra is unavailable:

```bash
uv run behave --tags=~@needs-redis
uv run behave --tags=@needs-postgres
```

## Do Not

- Share adapter instances or DB state across scenarios without cleanup.
- Write pytest suites as the primary ArchiPy app test style.
- Call real external services from untagged “unit” BDD scenarios.
